<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Communist Party of Vietnam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1930</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as CPV, Vietnamese Communist Party, Vietnam Workers' Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> is the ruling and only legal party of Vietnam. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh">Ho Chi Minh</a> in 1930 and soon renamed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochinese-communist-party">Indochinese Communist Party</a>, it led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and ruled North Vietnam as the Workers' Party from 1951. It took its present name in 1976 after reunification, and in 1986 launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doi-moi">Doi Moi</a> market reforms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-vietnam.jpg" alt="Communist Party of Vietnam" width="320" height="279" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original work by Eureka287, vector work by Lasse Havelund, final edit by ComradeBlots · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Communist_Party_of_Vietnam_flag_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
